1079 #uuid "b8009739-528a-5b9d-8b7a-977eb7894c6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421785 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421785 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162593" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421785 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421785 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421785 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f3288098-3c26-556d-b6c9-f206da47adfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421785 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩|}_{x=-v\\,y=-u\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,-2(-v),\\,-(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot 0+2v\\cdot (-2u)+u\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4uv-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4uv+u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{u}^{2}v+\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2v+\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{[{v}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}v]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Flux Through Parametric Surfaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186434834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434817 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "67831f4f-8138-536f-9514-23aeb5868445" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434818 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434818 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434818 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02b1374a-677b-550b-816a-6cbd02c5f061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434819 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb